<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I374f7e21cc25c335bdc42a49c7501a09ba0ea099" commit="d5ad874a93daab0af3ef0490cbb5375b4d884b7e" commit_message="FROMLIST: drm/bridge: analogix_dp: rename RK3288_DP to ROCKCHIP_DP  Rename RK3288_DP macros to ROCKCHIP_DP, prepare to add eDP support for more Rockchip chips.  Cc: Inki Dae &lt;inki.dae@samsung.com&gt; Cc: Mark Yao &lt;mark.yao@rock-chips.com&gt; Cc: Jingoo Han &lt;jingoohan1@gmail.com&gt; Cc: Thierry Reding &lt;thierry.reding@gmail.com&gt; Cc: Krzysztof Kozlowski &lt;k.kozlowski@samsung.com&gt; Cc: Heiko Stuebner &lt;heiko@sntech.de&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53565 TEST=Test eDP on rk3288-minnie  Change-Id: I374f7e21cc25c335bdc42a49c7501a09ba0ea099 Reviewed-by: Stphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; Tested-by: Javier Martinez Canillas &lt;javier@osg.samsung.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9175641/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346312 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346312" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="23" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/12/346312/23" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ieba941a0a5accd2687933b79a112215824d40e2a" commit="ead2b4e7b9b62505bd0c434e3b9b3e8af89d3c9b" commit_message="FROMLIST: drm/rockchip: analogix_dp: split the lcdc select setting into device data  eDP controller need to declare which vop provide the video source, and it's defined in GRF registers.  But different chips have different GRF register address, so we need to create a device data to declare the GRF messages for each chips.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53565 TEST=Test eDP on rk3399-gru  Change-Id: Ieba941a0a5accd2687933b79a112215824d40e2a Acked-by: Mark Yao &lt;mark.yao@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9175567/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346313 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346313" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="22" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/13/346313/22" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I72d87d4673191203cdefd68d7b057aa23ba84ae8" commit="7340c7c56e137baddd8b2fce2a4f3d0935873e26" commit_message="FROMLIST: drm/bridge: analogix_dp: correct the register bit define error in ANALOGIX_DP_PLL_REG_1  There're an register define error in ANALOGIX_DP_PLL_REG_1 which introduced by commit bcec20fd5ad6 (&quot;drm: bridge: analogix/dp: add some rk3288 special registers setting&quot;).  The PHY PLL input clock source is selected by ANALOGIX_DP_PLL_REG_1 BIT 0, not BIT 1.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53565 TEST=Test eDP on rk3399-gru  Change-Id: I72d87d4673191203cdefd68d7b057aa23ba84ae8 Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tomasz.figa@chromium.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; Tested-by: Javier Martinez Canillas &lt;javier@osg.samsung.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9175589/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346315 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346315" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="22" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/15/346315/22" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ic757140343878c0fb332dd546c7083302e275537" commit="ed63a56d86ce23c67ce0fc756b25e764de9ff407" commit_message="FROMLIST: drm/bridge: analogix_dp: some rockchip chips need to flip REF_CLK bit setting  As vendor document indicate, when REF_CLK bit set 0, then DP phy's REF_CLK should switch to 24M source clock.  But due to IC PHY layout mistaken, some chips need to flip this bit(like RK3288), and unfortunately they didn't indicate in the DP version register. That's why we have to make this little hack.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53565 TEST=Test eDP on rk3399-gru  Change-Id: Ic757140343878c0fb332dd546c7083302e275537 Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; Tested-by: Javier Martinez Canillas &lt;javier@osg.samsung.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9175637/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346852 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346852" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="19" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/52/346852/19" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="If013b238dd370a51f70a5ee9f30cd1ee22f49282" commit="c711a5231fda04f2af50de8cf8df17cb5acc7c21" commit_message="FROMLIST: drm/rockchip: analogix_dp: add rk3399 eDP support  RK3399 and RK3288 shared the same eDP IP controller, only some light difference with VOP configure and GRF configure.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53565 TEST=Test eDP on rk3399-gru  Change-Id: If013b238dd370a51f70a5ee9f30cd1ee22f49282 Acked-by: Mark Yao &lt;mark.yao@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9175585/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346314 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346314" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="22" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/14/346314/22" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ica5850995877ab56b94216a78c20c007b41197ac" commit="7dedd11595ca96265c72447226f76d78cedec41a" commit_message="FROMLIST: drm/rockchip: analogix_dp: make panel detect to an optional action  Some boards don't need to declare a panel device node, like the display interface is DP monitors, so it's necessary to make the panel detect to an optional action.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53565 TEST=Test eDP on rk3399-gru  Change-Id: Ica5850995877ab56b94216a78c20c007b41197ac Acked-by: Mark Yao &lt;mark.yao@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9175629/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346316 Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346316" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="22" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/16/346316/22" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I1ba48625abfed8d7fb7224e8694318e9fe20de88" commit="79426825f85be4deafcfccfbe60bf0a26d1edeb4" commit_message="FROMLIST: drm/bridge: analogix_dp: passing the connector as an argument in .get_modes()  It's better to pass the connector to platform driver in .get_modes() callback, just like what the .get_modes() helper function designed.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53565 TEST=Test eDP on rk3399-gru  Change-Id: I1ba48625abfed8d7fb7224e8694318e9fe20de88 Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9175581/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346317 Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346317" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="22" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/17/346317/22" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I1f6a61773ea8014d2de4e2efb597b36c273e4bb3" commit="16c67afefdcb95d6d6e9f69699880783a5ceb48b" commit_message="FROMLIST: drm/rockchip: analogix_dp: correct the connector display color format and bpc  Rockchip VOP couldn't output YUV video format for eDP controller, so when driver detect connector support YUV video format, we need to hack it down to RGB888.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53565 TEST=Test eDP on rk3399-gru  Change-Id: I1f6a61773ea8014d2de4e2efb597b36c273e4bb3 Acked-by: Mark Yao &lt;mark.yao@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9175601/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346318 Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346318" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="22" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/18/346318/22" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I8a84585011da2b527ff3e6ebc8809323f9958d31" commit="cfcf794f833e3b2a95caa9ab2f2b25a1d697ad81" commit_message="FROMLIST: drm/rockchip: analogix_dp: update the comments about why need to hardcode VOP output mode  The hardware IC designed that VOP must output the RGB10 video format to eDP contoller, and if eDP panel only support RGB8, then eDP contoller should cut down the video data, not via VOP contoller, that's why we need to hardcode the VOP output mode to RGA10 here.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53565 TEST=Test eDP on rk3399-gru  Change-Id: I8a84585011da2b527ff3e6ebc8809323f9958d31 Acked-by: Mark Yao &lt;mark.yao@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tomasz.figa@chromium.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9175603/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346853 Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346853" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="19" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/53/346853/19" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ia13b5aedb62383cdc9f7a5ab87ccd558b35ce7c6" commit="72941cefd82e6caba00e61fab71942945902ccc1" commit_message="FROMLIST: drm/bridge: analogix_dp: fix no drm hpd event when panel plug in  The enum value of DP_IRQ_TYPE_HP_CABLE_IN is zero, but driver only send drm hp event when the irq_type and the enum value is true.  if (irq_type &amp; DP_IRQ_TYPE_HP_CABLE_IN || ...)  drm_helper_hpd_irq_event(dp-&gt;drm_dev);  So there would no drm hpd event when cable plug in, to fix that just need to assign all hotplug enum with no-zero values.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53565 TEST=Test eDP on rk3399-gru  Change-Id: Ia13b5aedb62383cdc9f7a5ab87ccd558b35ce7c6 Reported-by: Dan Carpenter &lt;dan.carpenter@oracle.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; Tested-by: Javier Martinez Canillas &lt;javier@osg.samsung.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9175605/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346319 Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346319" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="22" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/19/346319/22" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icc77fe5d7da07ed0986e00fc05c80032056c3631" commit="c24f206e82ba62781afe414abca247e6cdd72b23" commit_message="login: Use android-data directory in /home/root.  We are moving android-data directory from the current fixed path (/home/chronos/user/android-data) to a path inside mounted cryptohome (/home/root/&lt;CryptohomeID&gt;/android-data).  Note that the parameter of StartArcInstance() D-Bus method has already been converted from socket_path to user_id in following Chrome change: https://codereview.chromium.org/2023803003/  CQ-DEPEND=CL:*264405 CQ-DEPEND=CL:*264339 CQ-DEPEND=CL:*261224 BUG=b:26700652 TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board $BOARD --packages chromeos-login  Change-Id: Icc77fe5d7da07ed0986e00fc05c80032056c3631 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/351130 Commit-Ready: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="351130" owner_email="nya@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/30/351130/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iae56f3773c8399c15607012fec4346cf37d50f6a" commit="1e702663be30ebfd319e4b7943bcdfce7164d7df" commit_message="login: RemoveArcData() removes new directory location  Revised Chrome-side change will send cryptohome ID with RemoveArcData D-Bus method call. https://codereview.chromium.org/1966133002/  BUG=b:26700652 TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board $BOARD --packages chromeos-login  Change-Id: Iae56f3773c8399c15607012fec4346cf37d50f6a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/352382 Commit-Ready: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: S